>> Edocrine system (hormone producers)
* Hypothalamus - an almond-sized gland in the middle of the brain, regulates other glands' hormone releases
* Pituitary - a  gland connected to the hypothalamus, releases some hormones (TODO - check which)
* Adrenal - glands atop the kidneys, create adrenaline
**  adrenaline increases heart and breathing rates
* Gonads - the testes/ovaries; release testosterone, estrogen, progesterone
* Pineal - a gland within the brain, releases melatonin
**  melatonin encourages rest
* Thyroid - gland in the throat, releases hormones that maintain homeostasis (growth, digestion, and various internal systems)




